/-!
# The three-matrix Gerstenhaber bound in characteristic zero

For any field of characteristic zero, three pairwise commuting square matrices
generate a unital algebra of dimension at most the size of the matrices.
The statement includes matrices of size zero. The published paper also treats
positive characteristic using a geometric argument; the formal result here
covers characteristic zero.
-/

/-- The unital algebra generated by a commuting triple has dimension at most n. -/
theorem Gerstenhaber.charZero_three_commuting_matrices {K : Type*} [Field K] [CharZero K]
    {n : ℕ} (A B C : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) K)
    (hAB : Commute A B) (hAC : Commute A C) (hBC : Commute B C) :
    Module.finrank K (Algebra.adjoin K ({A, B, C} : Set (Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) K))) ≤ n := by
  sorry
